meta {
  name: Manual Check-in
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/physical/sessions/{{physicalSessionId}}/check-ins
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "MANUAL",
    "studentId": "{{physicalStudentId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  #45, US-PHYSICAL-008 escenario 1. The endpoint is public at the filter
  level (`permitAll`) for both variants, but MANUAL requires a Bearer token
  with role RECEPTIONIST or ADMIN, verified inside the use case, not the
  security filter (D5) — `authToken` here must belong to a RECEPTIONIST or
  ADMIN user, and `physicalStudentId` must hold a confirmed capacity
  assignment for `physicalSessionId`.

  A MANUAL body must never carry any QR-only field (`qrCredentials`,
  `deviceId`, `deviceToken`) — mixing variants is rejected before the use
  case runs.

  Validation order (asserted by test): role → studentId existence →
  confirmed capacity assignment → session not CANCELLED → idempotent
  read-through → single Redis lock (shared with the QR variant on the same
  key) → INSERT.

  Success contract: 201 on the first valid MANUAL check-in, 200 on any
  repeat for the same student+session (no duplicate row, no lock acquired).
  Error contract:
    400 INVALID_REQUEST → malformed body, mixed QR/MANUAL fields, or a
        malformed studentId
    403 INSUFFICIENT_ROLE → caller is not RECEPTIONIST/ADMIN, or anonymous
    403 CAPACITY_ASSIGNMENT_REQUIRED → no confirmed assignment for the
        student — this INCLUDES an unknown {sessionId}: MANUAL resolves the
        assignment check before the session lookup, so an unknown session
        answers 403 here, never 404
    404 STUDENT_NOT_FOUND → studentId does not exist
    409 SESSION_NOT_ACTIVE → the session is CANCELLED (an already-elapsed
        but non-cancelled session is NOT rejected — MANUAL supports
        retroactive backfill with no time limit, deliberate divergence, D8)
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}
